# Charting a Castor EDC study with Dux and VegaLite

```elixir
# To use checkouts instead of the published packages, set
# CASTOR_EDC_DUX_PATH, CASTOR_EDC_KINO_PATH and CASTOR_EDC_PATH.
dux = System.get_env("CASTOR_EDC_DUX_PATH")
kino = System.get_env("CASTOR_EDC_KINO_PATH")
core = System.get_env("CASTOR_EDC_PATH")

Mix.install(
  [
    if(dux, do: {:ex_castor_edc_dux, path: dux}, else: {:ex_castor_edc_dux, "~> 0.1.0"}),
    if(kino, do: {:ex_castor_edc_kino, path: kino}, else: {:ex_castor_edc_kino, "~> 0.1.0"}),
    {:kino_dux, "~> 0.2.0"},
    {:kino_vega_lite, "~> 0.1.13"}
  ] ++ if(core, do: [{:ex_castor_edc, path: core, override: true}], else: [])
)
```

## Introduction

This notebook draws the charts a study usually needs: how enrolment is going, how complete and how missing the data is, how the surveys and queries stand, and how one variable is spread.
Each chart shapes its data in DuckDB with a few Dux verbs, and draws the rows that come back with a VegaLite spec; change them to suit your study.

## Connecting

Add your API credentials as Livebook secrets: `CASTOR_EDC_CLIENT_ID` and `CASTOR_EDC_CLIENT_SECRET`, which you can create on your [account settings page](https://data.castoredc.com/account/settings).
The connection cell below reads them from there, so they never appear in the notebook: pick the server your studies are on, and test the connection.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.CastorEDC.Kino.ConnectionCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
client =
  CastorEDC.new(
    client_id: System.fetch_env!("LB_CASTOR_EDC_CLIENT_ID"),
    client_secret: System.fetch_env!("LB_CASTOR_EDC_CLIENT_SECRET"),
    base_url: "https://data.castoredc.com"
  )
```

Then pick the study to chart; the cell lists the studies the client can reach.

